---
import AffiliateDisclosure from "../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "How We Pick Products | Findsera";
const description =
  "See how Findsera chooses practical products, checks prices, prioritizes clear retailer links, and explains tradeoffs.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/how-we-pick-products/">
  <section class="section-spacing">
    <div class="container-shell max-w-4xl">
      <span class="eyebrow">Methodology</span>
      <h1 class="mt-6 font-serif text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900 sm:text-6xl">
        How We Pick Products
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-700">
        Findsera publishes a limited set of decision guides. A recommendation needs a clear job, a meaningful tradeoff, and a reason not to buy it before a retailer link is considered.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-10">
    <div class="container-shell max-w-4xl">
      <AffiliateDisclosure />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-20">
    <div class="container-shell grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-black/6 bg-white p-6 shadow-card">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">1. Start with the decision</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-700">
          Each guide starts with the routine, budget, space limit, or compatibility question behind a purchase. The guide should remain useful even when a reader chooses not to buy any listed product.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-black/6 bg-white p-6 shadow-card">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">2. Include the limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-700">
          Every recommendation needs a realistic skip case. Compatibility, counter space, setup effort, maintenance, portability, and budget can all make an otherwise good product a poor fit.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-black/6 bg-white p-6 shadow-card">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">3. Publish only verified commerce details</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-700">
          A price, stock claim, or retailer-offer schema is shown only while it is within the normal verification window. When that window expires, readers are directed to the retailer for current details instead of seeing stale numbers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-black/6 bg-white p-6 shadow-card">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">4. Retailer links come after the analysis</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-700">
          Direct retailer paths reduce ambiguity, but they are secondary to the guide. A link is not a recommendation by itself, and an affiliate relationship never guarantees inclusion or placement.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-black/6 bg-white p-6 shadow-card lg:col-span-2">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">5. Keep the indexed site small</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-700">
          Findsera keeps its indexable content focused on maintained editorial guides and trust pages. Product, category, and tag reference pages remain available for visitors but are not promoted as standalone editorial articles.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-black/6 bg-white p-6 shadow-card lg:col-span-2">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900">6. Clear review scope and corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ink-700">
          Review notes rely on public product details, retailer paths, price-check dates, category context, and nearby alternatives. Hands-on testing or lab measurements are only mentioned when they actually apply. If a listing changes, a source link breaks, or a recommendation no longer fits, readers can send corrections through the contact page.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
